.TH rcc 1 "august 2026" "rookcc 1.0.0" "user commands"
.SH name
rcc \- standalone native c compiler
.SH use
.B rcc
.RI [ options ] " file.c ..."
.SH description
rcc preprocesses parses checks optimizes and writes native output in one program

it does not start another compiler assembler or linker
.SH options
.TP
.BI -o " file"
write output to file
.TP
.B -E
preprocess only
.TP
.B -S
write a machine code listing when the target supports it
.TP
.B -c
write an elf relocatable object
.TP
.B -run
compile and run a temporary native executable
.TP
.B --check
parse check and optimize without writing output
.TP
.B --emit-ir
write verified target independent ir
.TP
.BI -std= mode
select c90 c99 c11 c17 c23 gnu99 gnu11 gnu17 gnu23 or rcc
.TP
.BI --target= target
select x86_64 aarch64 or riscv64
.TP
.BI --sysroot= dir
use a target sysroot
.TP
.BR -O0 , " -O1" , " -O2" , " -O3" , " -Og" , " -Os" , " -Oz" , " -Ofast"
select optimization policy
.TP
.BR -I , " -iquote" , " -isystem" , " -D" , " -U"
control the preprocessor
.TP
.BR -L , " -l" , " -R" , " -Wl,-rpath,dir"
control native elf library and archive resolution
.TP
.B #pragma rcc link name
request a shared library from the source file
.TP
.B -static
write an executable without a program interpreter
.TP
.B -fPIC
with \fB-c\fR write an x86 64 pic object
.TP
.B -g
write dwarf 4 function line and symbol data for x86 64 output
.TP
.B --print-targets
list targets
.TP
.B --print-backends
list backend scope
.TP
.B --print-toolchain
show compiler registries
.TP
.B --version
show version and target information
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
show complete help
.SH gnu assembly
gnu modes accept asm __asm and __asm__ with operands constraints clobbers volatile and asm goto

supported templates are encoded by the x86 64 backend
.SH files
the default resource tree is /usr/local/share/rcc
